nk/toto-fx/commits/2ea5306153ba7cc7145566f151aae89dc5a7b7b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-17T06:36:18Z","email":"funk@Funks-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Funk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-17T06:36:18Z","email":"funk@Funks-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Funk"},"message":"Polish v0.3.0 changelog entry\n\nAdd before/after summary, deprecation table, bundle sizes, and lead framing to match v0.2.0 release-notes style.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4148de80bb32c34ac64fa237a6b6802081818b49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/git/trees/4148de80bb32c34ac64fa237a6b6802081818b49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/git/commits/2ea5306153ba7cc7145566f151aae89dc5a7b7b7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/a-funk/toto-fx/commit/2ea5306153ba7cc7145566f151aae89dc5a7b7b7","node_id":"C_kwDOSAUwK9oAKDJlYTUzMDYxNTNiYTdjYzcxNDU1NjZmMTUxYWFlODlkYzVhN2I3Yjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/a-funk/toto-fx/commit/ea31d43fb87bc0b97ef8535db327ef936a268c13","sha":"ea31d43fb87bc0b97ef8535db327ef936a268c13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/commits/ea31d43fb87bc0b97ef8535db327ef936a268c13"}],"sha":"2ea5306153ba7cc7145566f151aae89dc5a7b7b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/commits/2ea5306153ba7cc7145566f151aae89dc5a7b7b7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/commits/ea31d43fb87bc0b97ef8535db327ef936a268c13/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-17T06:30:25Z","email":"funk@Funks-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Funk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-17T06:30:25Z","email":"funk@Funks-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Funk"},"message":"Bump version to 0.3.0\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3862be88cd1fd5578457ed812dc469e263f35042","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/git/trees/3862be88cd1fd5578457ed812dc469e263f35042"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/git/commits/ea31d43fb87bc0b97ef8535db327ef936a268c13","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/a-funk/toto-fx/commit/ea31d43fb87bc0b97ef8535db327ef936a268c13","node_id":"C_kwDOSAUwK9oAKGVhMzFkNDNmYjg3YmMwYjk3ZWY4NTM1ZGIzMjdlZjkzNmEyNjhjMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/a-funk/toto-fx/commit/78aae4da3e995a69e861ddf651620444af2876f2","sha":"78aae4da3e995a69e861ddf651620444af2876f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/commits/78aae4da3e995a69e861ddf651620444af2876f2"}],"sha":"ea31d43fb87bc0b97ef8535db327ef936a268c13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/commits/ea31d43fb87bc0b97ef8535db327ef936a268c13"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11507011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/a-funk","id":11507011,"login":"a-funk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNTA3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/commits/78aae4da3e995a69e861ddf651620444af2876f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-16T03:15:16Z","email":"alexfunk1222@gmail.com","name":"a-funk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-16T03:15:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"v0.3.0: Unified Particle Pipeline (#2)\n\nPhase 1 of Unified Particle Pipeline plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Bring FX draw callbacks into unified master tick loop\n\nFX draw callbacks previously self-scheduled their own RAF chain\nindependently from the master tick. This caused two separate frame\nloops running simultaneously, making it impossible to do a single\ncanvas clear per frame.\n\nChanges:\n- Add fxDraw to _masterSubs flags\n- registerFxDraw() activates master tick instead of self-scheduling\n- deregisterFxDraw() clears fxDraw flag when last callback removed\n- Rename _tickFxDraw → _tickFxDrawInner (called by _masterTick)\n- Remove _fxDrawRAF self-scheduling variable\n\nAll three subsystems (particles, speed lines, FX draw) now run\nunder one RAF loop with one frame budget monitor.\n\nPhase 2a of Unified Particle Pipeline plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Migrate creation.js from direct RAF to registerFxDraw\n\nSix creation variants (materialize, portal, confetti-drop,\nsparkle-trail, butterfly-carry, grow) used rogue RAF loops with\ndirect getFxCtx() access, bypassing the engine''s master tick.\nThis made them invisible to adaptive quality monitoring and\ncaused a latent bug where interrupted animations would clearRect\nthe entire FX canvas, wiping other plugins'' rendering.\n\nChanges per variant:\n- Replace getFxCtx() + own RAF loop with registerFxDraw()\n- Move textAlign/textBaseline setup inside callback (save/restore)\n- Replace completion exit with deregisterFxDraw()\n- Remove clearRect from cleanup functions — deregistration handles it\n\nAll canvas-rendering plugins now go through the unified FX draw\ncallback system. No more rogue RAF loops in the plugin layer.\n\nPhase 2b of Unified Particle Pipeline plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Merge three canvases into one unified FX canvas\n\nRemoves animation-canvas (z:9998) and speed-lines-canvas (z:9996).\nAll rendering — particles, speed lines, and FX draw callbacks — now\ndraws to the single fx-canvas (z:9999) with one clear per frame.\n\nChanges:\n- Single ctx.clearRect at top of _masterTick before any subsystem\n- _tickParticlesInner uses getFxCtx() instead of separate canvas\n- _tickSpeedLinesInner uses getFxCtx() instead of speedCtx\n- _tickFxDrawInner no longer clears (master tick handles it)\n- Remove animation-canvas creation, resize handler, DOM element\n- Remove speed-lines-canvas creation, resize handler, DOM element\n- Remove CSS opacity transitions on speed-lines-canvas (redundant)\n- getCanvas() returns getFxCanvas() with debug deprecation warning\n- getSpeedCanvas() returns getFxCanvas() (deprecated)\n- spawnParticles/pushParticles/spawnSmoke/spawnFireTrail use FxCanvas\n- warmup() acquires single canvas instead of three\n- Net: -129 lines, +47 lines — significant simplification\n\nPhase 3 of Unified Particle Pipeline plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Convert spawnParticles to shared pool FX draw callback\n\nThe particle system is no longer a separate subsystem in _masterTick.\nInstead, a single registered FX draw callback (''particle-pool'')\nmanages the particle array with the same batch-rendering physics loop.\n\nChanges:\n- _particlePoolDraw registered as FX draw callback on first spawn\n- Deregisters when pool empties (0 alive particles)\n- spawnParticles/pushParticles/spawnSmoke/spawnFireTrail call\n  _ensureParticlePool() instead of legacy _tickParticles()\n- Remove particles from _masterSubs (now driven by fxDraw)\n- Remove particleRAF variable (no longer needed)\n- Remove _tickParticlesInner and _tickParticles functions\n- Batch rendering preserved: single font-bucket pass per frame\n- MAX_PARTICLES splice-oldest cap preserved in pushParticles\n\nOne rendering path for everything. spawnParticles is now a convenience\nwrapper over the FX draw callback system.\n\nPhase 4 of Unified Particle Pipeline plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add debug warnings, unified budget monitoring, and CHANGELOG for v0.3.0\n\nPhase 5 — observability and documentation for the unified pipeline:\n\n- configure({ debug: true }) enables debug mode in FX module\n- drawChar warns when alpha < 0.1 (once per char+size, debug only)\n- Master tick warns when entity count exceeds device budget (throttled)\n- Fix: getCanvas() deprecation now uses _fxDebug instead of undefined _config\n- CHANGELOG documents all v0.3.0 changes: canvas merge, pipeline\n  unification, creation.js migration, cute alpha bumps, deprecations\n\nPhase 5 of Unified Particle Pipeline plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update docs for v0.3.0 unified canvas architecture\n\nfx-api.md:\n- Canvas section: three canvases → one unified #fx-canvas\n- Deprecation notes for getCanvas() and getSpeedCanvas()\n- spawnParticles renders via shared pool draw callback\n- Speed lines render to unified canvas\n- Add debug option to configure()\n- Update warmup description\n\nplugin-guide.md:\n- Rendering Layers rewritten for unified architecture\n- Layer 1: note that particles + speed lines also render here\n- Layer 2: particles are internally a draw callback\n- Canvas Stack table: simplified to #fx-canvas + dotgrid\n- Added rules: no direct getFxCtx(), no rogue RAF, no clearRect\n- Updated combining layers section\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix bugs and doc issues from v0.3.0 first-time developer test\n\nCode fixes (engine.js):\n- Inject ctx.helpers in auto-created category dispatcher so plugins\n  can access FX utilities via ctx.helpers (Bug 2). Set via\n  createEngine({ helpers: FX }) or configure({ helpers: FX }).\n- Add stop-before-play guard in dispatcher to prevent stale\n  ANIM_KEY when rapidly switching animations on same element (Bug 4).\n\nDoc fixes (plugin-guide.md):\n- Fix getItemRect return shape: {cx, cy, rect: DOMRect} not\n  {cx, cy, width, height, top, left} (Bug 1)\n- Fix intensityScale range: 0.3-1.0 not 0.5-2.0 (Bug 3)\n- Add Debugging section documenting isIdle(), getAdaptiveQuality(),\n  fxConfig, and debug mode warnings\n\nDoc fixes (README.md):\n- Add IIFE custom plugin example showing engine.register() with\n  ctx.helpers pattern for script-tag users\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix stale README references for v0.3.0\n\n- Features: replace \"Canvas compositor\" with unified pipeline and\n  two-tool plugin model description\n- FX Quick Reference: fix spawnParticles params (colors→color,\n  speed→spread, add life/upBias to match actual API)\n- FX Quick Reference: fix getItemRect return shape ({cx, cy, rect})\n- Fix Deeper Reading link pointing to old v1.1-improvements branch\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Bump cute.js alpha multipliers for visible particle rendering\n\nCute animation variants (flowers, butterflies, bees, cats, dogs,\nsnowfall, ocean, fireflies) used manual alpha multipliers as low as\n0.3, making them nearly invisible on light themes. Raised 43 alpha\nvalues proportionally across 8 variants while preserving layer depth\nratios (veins still fainter than leaves, pebbles fainter than ground).\n\nKey changes:\n- Flower petals: lerp(0.35, 0.65) → lerp(0.55, 0.85)\n- Leaf alpha: lerp(0.4, 0.75) → lerp(0.55, 0.85)\n- Leaf veins: * 0.3 → * 0.5\n- Ground/pebbles: * 0.35 → * 0.55\n- Butterfly wings: * 0.7 → * 0.85\n- Bee parts: * 0.6 → * 0.75\n- Ocean waves: lerp(0.3, 0.7) → lerp(0.5, 0.85)\n- Firefly body: * 0.3 → * 0.5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Funk <funk@Funks-MacBook-Air.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"22864147e91c3d488cef8a81e6a9f9ad83d13ea0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/git/trees/22864147e91c3d488cef8a81e6a9f9ad83d13ea0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/git/commits/78aae4da3e995a69e861ddf651620444af2876f2","verification":{"payload":"tree 22864147e91c3d488cef8a81e6a9f9ad83d13ea0\nparent 330f5a1688a380c4e292b7470e8d8c78209d8a47\nauthor a-funk <alexfunk1222@gmail.com> 1776309316 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776309316 -0700\n\nv0.3.0: Unified Particle Pipeline (#2)\n\nPhase 1 of Unified Particle Pipeline plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Bring FX draw callbacks into unified master tick loop\n\nFX draw callbacks previously self-scheduled their own RAF chain\nindependently from the master tick. This caused two separate frame\nloops running simultaneously, making it impossible to do a single\ncanvas clear per frame.\n\nChanges:\n- Add fxDraw to _masterSubs flags\n- registerFxDraw() activates master tick instead of self-scheduling\n- deregisterFxDraw() clears fxDraw flag when last callback removed\n- Rename _tickFxDraw → _tickFxDrawInner (called by _masterTick)\n- Remove _fxDrawRAF self-scheduling variable\n\nAll three subsystems (particles, speed lines, FX draw) now run\nunder one RAF loop with one frame budget monitor.\n\nPhase 2a of Unified Particle Pipeline plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Migrate creation.js from direct RAF to registerFxDraw\n\nSix creation variants (materialize, portal, confetti-drop,\nsparkle-trail, butterfly-carry, grow) used rogue RAF loops with\ndirect getFxCtx() access, bypassing the engine''s master tick.\nThis made them invisible to adaptive quality monitoring and\ncaused a latent bug where interrupted animations would clearRect\nthe entire FX canvas, wiping other plugins'' rendering.\n\nChanges per variant:\n- Replace getFxCtx() + own RAF loop with registerFxDraw()\n- Move textAlign/textBaseline setup inside callback (save/restore)\n- Replace completion exit with deregisterFxDraw()\n- Remove clearRect from cleanup functions — deregistration handles it\n\nAll canvas-rendering plugins now go through the unified FX draw\ncallback system. No more rogue RAF loops in the plugin layer.\n\nPhase 2b of Unified Particle Pipeline plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Merge three canvases into one unified FX canvas\n\nRemoves animation-canvas (z:9998) and speed-lines-canvas (z:9996).\nAll rendering — particles, speed lines, and FX draw callbacks — now\ndraws to the single fx-canvas (z:9999) with one clear per frame.\n\nChanges:\n- Single ctx.clearRect at top of _masterTick before any subsystem\n- _tickParticlesInner uses getFxCtx() instead of separate canvas\n- _tickSpeedLinesInner uses getFxCtx() instead of speedCtx\n- _tickFxDrawInner no longer clears (master tick handles it)\n- Remove animation-canvas creation, resize handler, DOM element\n- Remove speed-lines-canvas creation, resize handler, DOM element\n- Remove CSS opacity transitions on speed-lines-canvas (redundant)\n- getCanvas() returns getFxCanvas() with debug deprecation warning\n- getSpeedCanvas() returns getFxCanvas() (deprecated)\n- spawnParticles/pushParticles/spawnSmoke/spawnFireTrail use FxCanvas\n- warmup() acquires single canvas instead of three\n- Net: -129 lines, +47 lines — significant simplification\n\nPhase 3 of Unified Particle Pipeline plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Convert spawnParticles to shared pool FX draw callback\n\nThe particle system is no longer a separate subsystem in _masterTick.\nInstead, a single registered FX draw callback (''particle-pool'')\nmanages the particle array with the same batch-rendering physics loop.\n\nChanges:\n- _particlePoolDraw registered as FX draw callback on first spawn\n- Deregisters when pool empties (0 alive particles)\n- spawnParticles/pushParticles/spawnSmoke/spawnFireTrail call\n  _ensureParticlePool() instead of legacy _tickParticles()\n- Remove particles from _masterSubs (now driven by fxDraw)\n- Remove particleRAF variable (no longer needed)\n- Remove _tickParticlesInner and _tickParticles functions\n- Batch rendering preserved: single font-bucket pass per frame\n- MAX_PARTICLES splice-oldest cap preserved in pushParticles\n\nOne rendering path for everything. spawnParticles is now a convenience\nwrapper over the FX draw callback system.\n\nPhase 4 of Unified Particle Pipeline plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add debug warnings, unified budget monitoring, and CHANGELOG for v0.3.0\n\nPhase 5 — observability and documentation for the unified pipeline:\n\n- configure({ debug: true }) enables debug mode in FX module\n- drawChar warns when alpha < 0.1 (once per char+size, debug only)\n- Master tick warns when entity count exceeds device budget (throttled)\n- Fix: getCanvas() deprecation now uses _fxDebug instead of undefined _config\n- CHANGELOG documents all v0.3.0 changes: canvas merge, pipeline\n  unification, creation.js migration, cute alpha bumps, deprecations\n\nPhase 5 of Unified Particle Pipeline plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update docs for v0.3.0 unified canvas architecture\n\nfx-api.md:\n- Canvas section: three canvases → one unified #fx-canvas\n- Deprecation notes for getCanvas() and getSpeedCanvas()\n- spawnParticles renders via shared pool draw callback\n- Speed lines render to unified canvas\n- Add debug option to configure()\n- Update warmup description\n\nplugin-guide.md:\n- Rendering Layers rewritten for unified architecture\n- Layer 1: note that particles + speed lines also render here\n- Layer 2: particles are internally a draw callback\n- Canvas Stack table: simplified to #fx-canvas + dotgrid\n- Added rules: no direct getFxCtx(), no rogue RAF, no clearRect\n- Updated combining layers section\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix bugs and doc issues from v0.3.0 first-time developer test\n\nCode fixes (engine.js):\n- Inject ctx.helpers in auto-created category dispatcher so plugins\n  can access FX utilities via ctx.helpers (Bug 2). Set via\n  createEngine({ helpers: FX }) or configure({ helpers: FX }).\n- Add stop-before-play guard in dispatcher to prevent stale\n  ANIM_KEY when rapidly switching animations on same element (Bug 4).\n\nDoc fixes (plugin-guide.md):\n- Fix getItemRect return shape: {cx, cy, rect: DOMRect} not\n  {cx, cy, width, height, top, left} (Bug 1)\n- Fix intensityScale range: 0.3-1.0 not 0.5-2.0 (Bug 3)\n- Add Debugging section documenting isIdle(), getAdaptiveQuality(),\n  fxConfig, and debug mode warnings\n\nDoc fixes (README.md):\n- Add IIFE custom plugin example showing engine.register() with\n  ctx.helpers pattern for script-tag users\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix stale README references for v0.3.0\n\n- Features: replace \"Canvas compositor\" with unified pipeline and\n  two-tool plugin model description\n- FX Quick Reference: fix spawnParticles params (colors→color,\n  speed→spread, add life/upBias to match actual API)\n- FX Quick Reference: fix getItemRect return shape ({cx, cy, rect})\n- Fix Deeper Reading link pointing to old v1.1-improvements branch\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Bump cute.js alpha multipliers for visible particle rendering\n\nCute animation variants (flowers, butterflies, bees, cats, dogs,\nsnowfall, ocean, fireflies) used manual alpha multipliers as low as\n0.3, making them nearly invisible on light themes. Raised 43 alpha\nvalues proportionally across 8 variants while preserving layer depth\nratios (veins still fainter than leaves, pebbles fainter than ground).\n\nKey changes:\n- Flower petals: lerp(0.35, 0.65) → lerp(0.55, 0.85)\n- Leaf alpha: lerp(0.4, 0.75) → lerp(0.55, 0.85)\n- Leaf veins: * 0.3 → * 0.5\n- Ground/pebbles: * 0.35 → * 0.55\n- Butterfly wings: * 0.7 → * 0.85\n- Bee parts: * 0.6 → * 0.75\n- Ocean waves: lerp(0.3, 0.7) → lerp(0.5, 0.85)\n- Firefly body: * 0.3 → * 0.5\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Funk <funk@Funks-MacBook-Air.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp4FRECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJy0QABnqC9hLGS9m8cYuhZ82Ur/n\nMrWQ7BDUNBPY5KgQOIiTKilb0tLkvyXM9Q16OI5ho57UgRJmxFJ+ebjmL4VYUq7G\nYWHmAiFEunG1Oo4FQekeFYctgRPTYxH2gb4DH06NmxvO8NbXRhJAbAr+Tb4OHCkU\nkz83s/4u2chgx01Y2p/bvObLFJ1wpZuqJrwYim4eD/BVOtjc9yoH5r2AXW8comMJ\nDmwk5bwvBicK9lMt9KCbB3IJ9WNv7dmP+zUDqfKOcFv+JlqaBYHbxrsOIWFN91Kf\nrAvvc7+BSLhpQHsWCQiA3bHDEjIyXp0eF9yUWz/DCWJSLFQ3JlClI2zFG+g29ZY+\nzvRmNQMRd0Or02PGJHXY+e0YC7BP8gjoyNFUM6U12mJ/BGkYZ2r6GyEg9cDBtk6H\n1tLWNOr6djpO9PPeSkAHCB7oG+9wN8YCQmnaY0s6O1dcwn1zsQDe03WR6dlCr1ma\n+CCV+h1Mt97NrHifjH6s9OMUlNzAlcG73Mxg3NwwiO8GmIa/Dnyxhez1pj3sEbj/\nwttAEeY5mQrR5q1XunmQ5gWPrHw2VBJOW8Yej1D8zjyHqX+w+mSqHxy2itaZ4Vp0\nqx1mWWGO+zYdGE2K006gBiG5lan/pxv0qP428et5gjMkcpGjiwNyh2mGlaRYn/D6\nRik4VJCkkkmCOMxAR746\n=dCNo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-16T03:15:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/a-funk/toto-fx/commit/78aae4da3e995a69e861ddf651620444af2876f2","node_id":"C_kwDOSAUwK9oAKDc4YWFlNGRhM2U5OTVhNjllODYxZGRmNjUxNjIwNDQ0YWYyODc2ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/a-funk/toto-fx/commit/330f5a1688a380c4e292b7470e8d8c78209d8a47","sha":"330f5a1688a380c4e292b7470e8d8c78209d8a47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/commits/330f5a1688a380c4e292b7470e8d8c78209d8a47"}],"sha":"78aae4da3e995a69e861ddf651620444af2876f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/commits/78aae4da3e995a69e861ddf651620444af2876f2"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/commits/330f5a1688a380c4e292b7470e8d8c78209d8a47/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-15T19:03:29Z","email":"funk@Funks-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Funk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-15T19:03:29Z","email":"funk@Funks-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Funk"},"message":"Fix typos in README and CHANGELOG for v0.2.0 release\n\n- README: \"a Animation\" → \"an Animation\", \"arcitectural\" → \"architectural\"\n- CHANGELOG: debug default entry now correctly says false\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8f179dd3309f84312eaf3a97f829b7271b04662d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/git/trees/8f179dd3309f84312eaf3a97f829b7271b04662d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/git/commits/330f5a1688a380c4e292b7470e8d8c78209d8a47","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/a-funk/toto-fx/commit/330f5a1688a380c4e292b7470e8d8c78209d8a47","node_id":"C_kwDOSAUwK9oAKDMzMGY1YTE2ODhhMzgwYzRlMjkyYjc0NzBlOGQ4Yzc4MjA5ZDhhNDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/a-funk/toto-fx/commit/0388aeb7557f09d90ca7e999cdeff742da901d0c","sha":"0388aeb7557f09d90ca7e999cdeff742da901d0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/commits/0388aeb7557f09d90ca7e999cdeff742da901d0c"}],"sha":"330f5a1688a380c4e292b7470e8d8c78209d8a47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/commits/330f5a1688a380c4e292b7470e8d8c78209d8a47"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/commits/0388aeb7557f09d90ca7e999cdeff742da901d0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-15T07:32:33Z","email":"funk@Funks-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Funk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-15T07:32:33Z","email":"funk@Funks-MacBook-Air.local","name":"Funk"},"message":"Default debug to false — OSS libraries should not emit console warnings without opt-in\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"327b6ecfb7d91d113df99d327f1eb9fc044b04e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/git/trees/327b6ecfb7d91d113df99d327f1eb9fc044b04e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/git/commits/0388aeb7557f09d90ca7e999cdeff742da901d0c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/a-funk/toto-fx/commit/0388aeb7557f09d90ca7e999cdeff742da901d0c","node_id":"C_kwDOSAUwK9oAKDAzODhhZWI3NTU3ZjA5ZDkwY2E3ZTk5OWNkZWZmNzQyZGE5MDFkMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/a-funk/toto-fx/commit/2860f4fff8e53c0b1f7b7e98a0f6f178a8743105","sha":"2860f4fff8e53c0b1f7b7e98a0f6f178a8743105","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/commits/2860f4fff8e53c0b1f7b7e98a0f6f178a8743105"}],"sha":"0388aeb7557f09d90ca7e999cdeff742da901d0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/commits/0388aeb7557f09d90ca7e999cdeff742da901d0c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11507011?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/a-funk","id":11507011,"login":"a-funk","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNTA3MDEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-funk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/commits/2860f4fff8e53c0b1f7b7e98a0f6f178a8743105/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-14T10:30:40Z","email":"alexfunk1222@gmail.com","name":"a-funk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-14T10:30:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"v0.2.0: Dotgrid plugin system, engine API improvements, framework integrations\n\n* v1.1: Isolated state, Symbol keys, events, reduced motion, error boundaries\n\n- StateStore and DOMObserver are now factory functions (createStateStore,\n  createDOMObserver) so each engine gets isolated state. Backwards-compat\n  singletons kept but deprecated.\n- Animation handles use Symbol key (ANIM_KEY) instead of __totoAnimation\n  string property — no collision with user code or serialization.\n- Engine emits lifecycle events: animationStart, animationEnd, reconcile.\n- reducedMotion config option passes ctx.reducedMotion to all play() calls.\n- Reconciler wraps _startElement in try/catch — one broken plugin can''t\n  kill all animations.\n- DOM observer watches data-anim-id attribute changes for morph engines\n  that patch in-place.\n- Configurable debounceMs for refresh coordinator.\n- Plugin lint fixes: const → let where variables are reassigned.\n- TypeScript types and docs updated. Tests for all new features.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add stop() callback to categories and document reconciler contract\n\nCategories now support an optional stop() callback that undoes what\nplay() did. engine.clear() calls stop() automatically — no more manual\nCSS cleanup. The reconciler also calls stop() before re-applying\nanimations on version change.\n\nREADME now documents ANIM_KEY handle, version tracking, when play()\nand stop() are called, and phase continuity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix register() → play() dispatch and normalize plugin install functions\n\nregister() stored variants into _variantRegistry but nothing read it —\nplay() and the reconciler only dispatched through _categories. This made\nthe documented IIFE quickstart silently do nothing.\n\nregister() now auto-creates a category dispatcher that looks up variants\nat call time, so play(), set(), and clear() all work after a single\nregister() call. Multiple styles under one category (thud + cute both\nunder ''action'') work without merge logic.\n\nAlso fixes cute, death, and creation plugin install() functions which\ncalled engine.registerCategory() with 3 args (engine only accepts 2),\nsilently corrupting the category map. All plugins now use the dual\npattern: register() for engines, registerCategory() for AnimationRegistry.\n\nReconciler _startElement fallback updated to call variant.play() instead\nof the nonexistent variant.start().\n\nIncludes test-drive.html demo page exercising all categories.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update README: register() docs, variant lookup table, persist quickstart\n\n- Rewrite register() vs registerCategory() section to reflect that\n  register() is the standard plugin path with auto-dispatch\n- Add category/style/variant quick reference table so developers don''t\n  have to guess style names from section headers\n- Add persist animation example (set/clear) to the IIFE quickstart\n- Clarify that install() calls register() which wires everything up\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add engine flow diagram to README intro\n\nASCII diagram showing the reconciliation pipeline:\nsemantic key → registry → resolver → swap detection → animation resumed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update README.md\n\n* Update README.md\n\n* Delete test-drive.html\n\n* Update README with full-featured Getting Started example and destroy→action changes\n\nReplace the minimal CSS-highlight Getting Started example with a complete\nanime-slam demo that includes dotgrid fluid simulation, plugin loading,\nFX wiring, and particle effects. Update ESM equivalent to match. Also\nupdate all variant tables, category references, and plugin docs to reflect\ndestroy variants being collapsed under the action category.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add variant cheatsheet with descriptions for all 59 animations\n\nNew doc at docs/variant-cheatsheet.md with one-sentence descriptions\nof every built-in variant, organized by category and style, with\ncopy-paste usage examples for each.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Collapse destroy category into action with style ''destroy''\n\nDestroy animations are conceptually action animations — the distinction\nbetween completing and destroying a card is which animation you pick,\nnot a different engine category. This moves all 11 destroy variants\n(explode, lightning, shredder, etc.) from category ''destroy''/style ''death''\nto category ''action''/style ''destroy''.\n\nThe plugin file (death.js), export names (deathPlugin, TotoFXDeath), and\nimport paths (toto-fx/plugins/death) are unchanged for backwards compat.\nOnly the registration routing and user-facing style name changed.\n\nUsage before: engine.play(''destroy'', el, { params: { style: ''death'', variant: ''explode'' } })\nUsage after:  engine.play(''action'', el, { params: { style: ''destroy'', variant: ''explode'' } })\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Clarify plugin install comment in Getting Started example\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Use engine.use() instead of plugin.install() in all IIFE examples\n\nengine.use() already supports plugin objects with install() methods,\nso IIFE and ESM usage is now consistent: engine.use(plugin) in both.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Delete test-drive.html\n\n* Add debug + sub-element docs to Getting Started, add test-drive demo page\n\nGetting Started now recommends debug: true and documents the four\noptional fx sub-elements (shadow, burst, badge, strike) that enhance\nanimation visuals. Test-drive page exercises all plugin categories\nwith a dotgrid background.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add engine events, accessibility, and migration docs for v1.1\n\nNew docs covering the three major documentation gaps identified in\nthe v1.1 audit: engine lifecycle events (on/off API), reduced motion\naccessibility support, and a v1.0-to-v1.1 migration guide. README\nupdated with narrative sections and multi-engine isolation example.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Delete test-drive.html\n\n* Make long code blocks collapsible, fix stale install() call in ESM example\n\nWrap 6 long code blocks in <details> tags to reduce visual noise:\nGetting Started HTML, ESM equivalent, Quickstart, FX Quick Reference,\nIndividual Module Exports, and Security Model. Also fix\nthudPlugin.install(engine) → engine.use(thudPlugin) in ESM example.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revert collapsible sections — details/summary renders poorly on dark themes\n\nThe <details> dropdowns were too subtle on GitHub dark mode, easy to\nmiss as interactive elements. Reverted all 6 collapsible sections back\nto plain headings and restored heading levels in the Security Model\nsection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add heart-pulse animation plugin and dotgrid heart effect\n\nNew dotgrid effect using implicit heart equation (x²+y²-1)³-x²y³=0\nwith multi-beat pulsing velocity injection. New heart-pulse plugin\n(action/love) pairs the dotgrid effect with a card scale throb.\n\nAlso includes prior session work: debug default to true, variant\ndiscovery methods (getStyles/getVariants/getParams), batch clear,\nclearAll, setDotgrid, FX.resetDotgrid, and test-drive demo page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add dotgrid plugin system with grid context, runEffect dispatch, and ctx injection\n\nDotgrid effects can now be registered as plugins via grid.use(plugin),\nmirroring the animation plugin architecture. Plugins receive a grid\ncontext object with getters for density/velocity arrays and helpers.\n\n- grid.registerEffect(), grid.use(), grid.runEffect(), grid.getEffectNames()\n- engine.dotgridEffect() + ctx.dotgridEffect injected into animation play context\n- Generic FX.doDotgridEffect(name, args) dispatcher replaces hardcoded switch\n- Heart effect extracted from dotgrid.js into standalone 2.6KB dotgrid plugin\n- heart-pulse animation plugin uses ctx.dotgridEffect (IIFE-safe)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Extract all dotgrid effects into standalone plugins (phase 2)\n\nRipple, vortex, crater, nuclear, and scorch effects moved from\ndotgrid.js into individual plugin files under src/dotgrid-plugins/.\ndotgrid.js drops from 19.5KB to 15.0KB. Each plugin is 1.8-2.6KB\nstandalone with zero bundled dependencies.\n\nBackward-compat wrappers (grid.ripple(), FX.doDotgridRipple, etc.)\npreserved — they delegate to runEffect() internally.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add dotgrid step() API and Remotion demo video project\n\nstep() enables frame-by-frame rendering without RAF — one-shot\nphysics + draw cycle for deterministic output in Remotion, tests,\nor any external frame driver. No changes to existing behavior.\n\nRemotion project (video/) includes 8 reusable components, 6 scenes\nwith actual toto-fx code and build output, and DotgridLive.tsx that\nrenders the real fluid sim live using grid.step().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Bump version to 0.2.0, fix debug default in types\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add React, Vue, and Svelte framework integrations\n\nThree thin wrapper packages for toto-fx:\n\ntoto-fx-react (10 files):\n  TotoFXProvider, useTotoFX, usePlay, usePersist, useAnimationRef,\n  useDotgridEffect, useEngineEvent, TotoFXDotgrid component.\n  Uses useSyncExternalStore for tear-free reactivity.\n\ntoto-fx-vue (10 files):\n  TotoFXPlugin, composables (useTotoFX, usePlay, usePersist,\n  useDotgridEffect), directives (v-toto-action, v-toto-persist),\n  TotoFXDotgrid SFC.\n\ntoto-fx-svelte (8 files):\n  Context (initTotoFX/getTotoFX), actions (totoAction, totoPersist,\n  totoDotgridEffect), createAnimationStore, TotoFXDotgrid component.\n\nAll packages are peer-dep only (zero bundled dependencies), follow\neach framework''s idiomatic patterns, and share the same engine\ninstance via provider/plugin/context.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add community preview READMEs for framework integrations\n\nEach README includes a community preview disclaimer noting the\npackages are untested and uncompiled, plus quick start examples\nand API reference tables.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add CHANGELOG, conceptual overview doc, update migration guide\n\nCHANGELOG.md covers all 0.2.0 changes with breaking changes,\nnew features, bundle sizes, and deprecations.\n\ndocs/what-is-toto-fx.md is a technical overview for developers:\narchitecture diagram, reconciler flow, plugin contracts, dotgrid\nfluid sim internals, framework-agnostic design, bundle architecture.\n\nMigration guide updated to cover 0.2.0 additions: dotgrid plugin\nsystem, new engine APIs, debug default change, framework integrations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Funk <funk@Funks-MacBook-Air.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6a59855be2da14aa2e9359ee32aca8d06fc18b02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/git/trees/6a59855be2da14aa2e9359ee32aca8d06fc18b02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/a-funk/toto-fx/git/commits/2860f4fff8e53c0b1f7b7e98a0f6f178a8743105","verification":{"payload":"tree 6a59855be2da14aa2e9359ee32aca8d06fc18b02\nparent e577598f60069f4dc4e8772f625865f4f835bf1b\nauthor a-funk <alexfunk1222@gmail.com> 1776162640 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776162640 -0700\n\nv0.2.0: Dotgrid plugin system, engine API improvements, framework integrations\n\n* v1.1: Isolated state, Symbol keys, events, reduced motion, error boundaries\n\n- StateStore and DOMObserver are now factory functions (createStateStore,\n  createDOMObserver) so each engine gets isolated state. Backwards-compat\n  singletons kept but deprecated.\n- Animation handles use Symbol key (ANIM_KEY) instead of __totoAnimation\n  string property — no collision with user code or serialization.\n- Engine emits lifecycle events: animationStart, animationEnd, reconcile.\n- reducedMotion config option passes ctx.reducedMotion to all play() calls.\n- Reconciler wraps _startElement in try/catch — one broken plugin can''t\n  kill all animations.\n- DOM observer watches data-anim-id attribute changes for morph engines\n  that patch in-place.\n- Configurable debounceMs for refresh coordinator.\n- Plugin lint fixes: const → let where variables are reassigned.\n- TypeScript types and docs updated. Tests for all new features.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add stop() callback to categories and document reconciler contract\n\nCategories now support an optional stop() callback that undoes what\nplay() did. engine.clear() calls stop() automatically — no more manual\nCSS cleanup. The reconciler also calls stop() before re-applying\nanimations on version change.\n\nREADME now documents ANIM_KEY handle, version tracking, when play()\nand stop() are called, and phase continuity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix register() → play() dispatch and normalize plugin install functions\n\nregister() stored variants into _variantRegistry but nothing read it —\nplay() and the reconciler only dispatched through _categories. This made\nthe documented IIFE quickstart silently do nothing.\n\nregister() now auto-creates a category dispatcher that looks up variants\nat call time, so play(), set(), and clear() all work after a single\nregister() call. Multiple styles under one category (thud + cute both\nunder ''action'') work without merge logic.\n\nAlso fixes cute, death, and creation plugin install() functions which\ncalled engine.registerCategory() with 3 args (engine only accepts 2),\nsilently corrupting the category map. All plugins now use the dual\npattern: register() for engines, registerCategory() for AnimationRegistry.\n\nReconciler _startElement fallback updated to call variant.play() instead\nof the nonexistent variant.start().\n\nIncludes test-drive.html demo page exercising all categories.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update README: register() docs, variant lookup table, persist quickstart\n\n- Rewrite register() vs registerCategory() section to reflect that\n  register() is the standard plugin path with auto-dispatch\n- Add category/style/variant quick reference table so developers don''t\n  have to guess style names from section headers\n- Add persist animation example (set/clear) to the IIFE quickstart\n- Clarify that install() calls register() which wires everything up\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add engine flow diagram to README intro\n\nASCII diagram showing the reconciliation pipeline:\nsemantic key → registry → resolver → swap detection → animation resumed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update README.md\n\n* Update README.md\n\n* Delete test-drive.html\n\n* Update README with full-featured Getting Started example and destroy→action changes\n\nReplace the minimal CSS-highlight Getting Started example with a complete\nanime-slam demo that includes dotgrid fluid simulation, plugin loading,\nFX wiring, and particle effects. Update ESM equivalent to match. Also\nupdate all variant tables, category references, and plugin docs to reflect\ndestroy variants being collapsed under the action category.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add variant cheatsheet with descriptions for all 59 animations\n\nNew doc at docs/variant-cheatsheet.md with one-sentence descriptions\nof every built-in variant, organized by category and style, with\ncopy-paste usage examples for each.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Collapse destroy category into action with style ''destroy''\n\nDestroy animations are conceptually action animations — the distinction\nbetween completing and destroying a card is which animation you pick,\nnot a different engine category. This moves all 11 destroy variants\n(explode, lightning, shredder, etc.) from category ''destroy''/style ''death''\nto category ''action''/style ''destroy''.\n\nThe plugin file (death.js), export names (deathPlugin, TotoFXDeath), and\nimport paths (toto-fx/plugins/death) are unchanged for backwards compat.\nOnly the registration routing and user-facing style name changed.\n\nUsage before: engine.play(''destroy'', el, { params: { style: ''death'', variant: ''explode'' } })\nUsage after:  engine.play(''action'', el, { params: { style: ''destroy'', variant: ''explode'' } })\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Clarify plugin install comment in Getting Started example\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Use engine.use() instead of plugin.install() in all IIFE examples\n\nengine.use() already supports plugin objects with install() methods,\nso IIFE and ESM usage is now consistent: engine.use(plugin) in both.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Delete test-drive.html\n\n* Add debug + sub-element docs to Getting Started, add test-drive demo page\n\nGetting Started now recommends debug: true and documents the four\noptional fx sub-elements (shadow, burst, badge, strike) that enhance\nanimation visuals. Test-drive page exercises all plugin categories\nwith a dotgrid background.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add engine events, accessibility, and migration docs for v1.1\n\nNew docs covering the three major documentation gaps identified in\nthe v1.1 audit: engine lifecycle events (on/off API), reduced motion\naccessibility support, and a v1.0-to-v1.1 migration guide. README\nupdated with narrative sections and multi-engine isolation example.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Delete test-drive.html\n\n* Make long code blocks collapsible, fix stale install() call in ESM example\n\nWrap 6 long code blocks in <details> tags to reduce visual noise:\nGetting Started HTML, ESM equivalent, Quickstart, FX Quick Reference,\nIndividual Module Exports, and Security Model. Also fix\nthudPlugin.install(engine) → engine.use(thudPlugin) in ESM example.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revert collapsible sections — details/summary renders poorly on dark themes\n\nThe <details> dropdowns were too subtle on GitHub dark mode, easy to\nmiss as interactive elements. Reverted all 6 collapsible sections back\nto plain headings and restored heading levels in the Security Model\nsection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add heart-pulse animation plugin and dotgrid heart effect\n\nNew dotgrid effect using implicit heart equation (x²+y²-1)³-x²y³=0\nwith multi-beat pulsing velocity injection. New heart-pulse plugin\n(action/love) pairs the dotgrid effect with a card scale throb.\n\nAlso includes prior session work: debug default to true, variant\ndiscovery methods (getStyles/getVariants/getParams), batch clear,\nclearAll, setDotgrid, FX.resetDotgrid, and test-drive demo page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add dotgrid plugin system with grid context, runEffect dispatch, and ctx injection\n\nDotgrid effects can now be registered as plugins via grid.use(plugin),\nmirroring the animation plugin architecture. Plugins receive a grid\ncontext object with getters for density/velocity arrays and helpers.\n\n- grid.registerEffect(), grid.use(), grid.runEffect(), grid.getEffectNames()\n- engine.dotgridEffect() + ctx.dotgridEffect injected into animation play context\n- Generic FX.doDotgridEffect(name, args) dispatcher replaces hardcoded switch\n- Heart effect extracted from dotgrid.js into standalone 2.6KB dotgrid plugin\n- heart-pulse animation plugin uses ctx.dotgridEffect (IIFE-safe)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Extract all dotgrid effects into standalone plugins (phase 2)\n\nRipple, vortex, crater, nuclear, and scorch effects moved from\ndotgrid.js into individual plugin files under src/dotgrid-plugins/.\ndotgrid.js drops from 19.5KB to 15.0KB. Each plugin is 1.8-2.6KB\nstandalone with zero bundled dependencies.\n\nBackward-compat wrappers (grid.ripple(), FX.doDotgridRipple, etc.)\npreserved — they delegate to runEffect() internally.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add dotgrid step() API and Remotion demo video project\n\nstep() enables frame-by-frame rendering without RAF — one-shot\nphysics + draw cycle for deterministic output in Remotion, tests,\nor any external frame driver. No changes to existing behavior.\n\nRemotion project (video/) includes 8 reusable components, 6 scenes\nwith actual toto-fx code and build output, and DotgridLive.tsx that\nrenders the real fluid sim live using grid.step().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Bump version to 0.2.0, fix debug default in types\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add React, Vue, and Svelte framework integrations\n\nThree thin wrapper packages for toto-fx:\n\ntoto-fx-react (10 files):\n  TotoFXProvider, useTotoFX, usePlay, usePersist, useAnimationRef,\n  useDotgridEffect, useEngineEvent, TotoFXDotgrid component.\n  Uses useSyncExternalStore for tear-free reactivity.\n\ntoto-fx-vue (10 files):\n  TotoFXPlugin, composables (useTotoFX, usePlay, usePersist,\n  useDotgridEffect), directives (v-toto-action, v-toto-persist),\n  TotoFXDotgrid SFC.\n\ntoto-fx-svelte (8 files):\n  Context (initTotoFX/getTotoFX), actions (totoAction, totoPersist,\n  totoDotgridEffect), createAnimationStore, TotoFXDotgrid component.\n\nAll packages are peer-dep only (zero bundled dependencies), follow\neach framework''s idiomatic patterns, and share the same engine\ninstance via provider/plugin/context.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add community preview READMEs for framework integrations\n\nEach README includes a community preview disclaimer noting the\npackages are untested and uncompiled, plus quick start examples\nand API reference tables.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add CHANGELOG, conceptual overview doc, update migration guide\n\nCHANGELOG.md covers all 0.2.0 changes with breaking changes,\nnew features, bundle sizes, and deprecations.\n\ndocs/what-is-toto-fx.md is a technical overview for developers:\narchitecture diagram, reconciler flow, plugin contracts, dotgrid\nfluid sim internals, framework-agnostic design, bundle architecture.\n\nMigration guide updated to cover 0.2.0 additions: dotgrid plugin\nsystem, new engine APIs, debug default change, framework integrations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Funk <funk@Funks-MacBook-Air.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp3hdRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIkUQAEl7Gz/yQ2dLmgm6JcJ4H3kR\n+3emGR2qT9F8uLnoGqTgn+zg4sscXnqh8zAtPu2RwYIrKdXbJz+xmbZmPRvJcd1V\ncMMjeo1TZ964vsG7FjHlodq79LUk7jwMejGhb7HoOghrtX617I78NwdlnJKxQtlv\nCpt0UMmU6hcBZld3GjbTtTl7+Xm8GECRJq62h+E+0sNa4TRN2/YDLBW2urZ6JJMa\nE3z2WlGUYaGcXLswnoGchmh3a+9GaNkkVXIL7JeHCQEDF2vqAAnuP51ZS7OsJSy5\npArWxYj9gKqe60BDmyEha+ticjrKI1AXJ7JqhQBtuHLZXrsihuTjISictufIjD5/\nxBbcK2L7wnVKK2na+osF0X9Ge28sz4yg0fuiWs9Sbp0D3N6jIeqMF3rW9KVRfmtM\nrP8VG+qt5Kv90IOwy1fhXYoAFOUhUQByU5ZjNYNG6wmf3EG3I9udWHj97Frx9Sq4\nZYJ3XXG3c3+bWO8mffwlLyS+/7JcNKH40POaEc+bqai6cyJPTpilgy0cuBgqE9iI\nCpFdTmXrUHmnThyDWmxb+h+0uoPoV/JCDljdPIyuCTp2jK6DwjQZX1PWXKQVwMzF\nb/e98sSl1WJfN7enZJ3Z8wgAlhOBzNRZRVHB1GvcXHrZMv8nQ6XP62bC6HeOLf5t\n8w3yvVFGB/4UtX1nvsZB\n=DoNT\n----