Danendz","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Danendz/vite-dev-tools/commits/500a007d5125e06c29bbd5b116a03ab63c4e78ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-19T09:00:28Z","email":"danilapayne@gmail.com","name":"Danendz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-19T09:00:28Z","email":"danilapayne@gmail.com","name":"Danendz"},"message":"feat: error attribution with source map resolution, badges, and console improvements\n\n- Add error/warning attribution: match console errors to owning components via stack trace file matching\n- Add source map resolution for stack frames via Vite HMR (preserves Vue SFC query strings)\n- Add error count badges on tree nodes with severity coloring (red=errors, amber=warnings-only)\n- Add error boundary detection (shield badge) for React class boundaries and Vue onErrorCaptured\n- Smart badge visibility: show subtree count when collapsed, own-only when expanded\n- Re-attribute errors on every tree update to handle Vue''s nodeId resets\n- Preserve existing attribution when duplicate entries are grouped\n- Add errors/warnings section in detail panel with stack traces\n- Add \"Copy for AI\" enriched clipboard format with error context\n- Add MCP tools: getConsoleErrors, getErrorContext\n- Add \"Clear on hot reload\" console setting (clears errors/warnings on HMR update)\n- Strip Vite cache-busting timestamps while preserving Vue module specifiers in source map lookups\n- Fix Vue SFC endLineNumber off-by-one (trailing newline)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a3d95496177a7c4f7dd89862f01f4fa598f9f54b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Danendz/vite-dev-tools/git/trees/a3d95496177a7c4f7dd89862f01f4fa598f9f54b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Danendz/vite-dev-tools/git/commits/500a007d5125e06c29bbd5b116a03ab63c4e78ce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"a