/users/EduardoMolinar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EduardoMolinar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EduardoMolinar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EduardoMolinar/kick-platform/commits/b148b5e6ee79d7f0fa146cf3c4c3bda7cfc792ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T00:35:23Z","email":"eduardomolinar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Eduardo Molinar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T00:35:23Z","email":"eduardomolinar@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Eduardo Molinar"},"message":"fix(ci): exclude remotes/* from shell sync to prevent --delete wipeout\n\nThe shell deploy runs `aws s3 sync dist/.../browser/ s3://bucket/ --delete`\nat the bucket root. Without an exclude on `remotes/*`, --delete treats\nevery file under /remotes/<name>/ as orphan (since none exist in the\nshell''s browser dist) and wipes them all.\n\nThe remote-deploy workflow already scopes its own --delete to its own\n/remotes/<name>/ subtree, so the safe contract is: shell never touches\n/remotes/*, each remote owns its prefix exclusively.\n\nThis is what caused the \"remote deploys passed green but bucket has no\nremotes\" symptom — the parallel remote uploads completed successfully,\nthen the shell deploy ran last and deleted everything they uploaded.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"11264df281b5de8011b3384534bd80ca577393d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EduardoMolinar/kick-platform/git/trees/11264df281b5de8011b3384534bd80ca577393d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EduardoMolinar/kick-platform/git/commits/b148b5e6ee79d7f0fa146cf3c4c3bda7cfc792ad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24195935?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EduardoMolinar/events{/privacy}","fol